  "caption": "Quinn's gorgeous new shoes were half a size too small. By hour three, the toes were filing complaints.\n\nIngrown nails, corns and calluses usually come from pressure and friction. Skin thickens where load piles up, so treating only the spot often means it comes back.\n\nWhat often helps: shoes with enough toe box width and length, cutting nails straight across, and building walking or running gradually. Skip the razors and DIY nail removal; a podiatrist can help with painful corns and ingrown nails. A sore foot can change how you walk, so new knee or hip aches are worth a look too.\n\nSpreading redness, pus or fever needs same-day care, and anyone with diabetes or poor circulation should get foot problems checked early.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
